  {
   "id": "9x0u3v_4tcIJ",
   "from": "Joe Cheng",
   "author": "ca443e6eaa0e78ed",
   "date": "2015-06-03T19:56:11Z",
   "subject": "Re: Multiple column names using TextInput",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Definitely don&#39;t use `cat()`, that won&#39;t help you at all.<br><br><div>That aside, input$value will be a single-element character vector--you probably want a character vector with one element per column. Take a look at the strsplit function, for example if the column names are space separated it&#39;d be cols &lt;- strsplit(input$value, &quot; &quot;)[[1]]. Or if separated by commas with optional whitespace, then cols &lt;- strsplit(input$value, &quot;\\\\s*,\\\\s*&quot;)[[1]].</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Wed, Jun 3, 2015 at 10:38 AM Santhana Krishnan &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">a.sant...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
